---
description: Respect ProjectBrain theme system (data-theme) in UI styling
alwaysApply: true
---

## Theme system (ProjectBrain)

- Themes are applied by setting `data-theme` on `<html>` (not via Tailwind `dark` class).
- See `projectbrain.frontend/src/_components/theme-provider.tsx` and `theme-initializer.tsx`.
- Theme overrides live in:
  - `projectbrain.frontend/src/styles/themes/dark.css`
  - `projectbrain.frontend/src/styles/themes/colourful.css`

## Rules

- Prefer **theme-aware utility classes** that are overridden in theme CSS (e.g. `bg-white`, `text-gray-900`, `text-gray-600`, `border-gray-300`, `bg-gray-100`, `bg-gray-200`, `hover:bg-gray-100`, `shadow`).
- **Do not rely on Tailwind `dark:*` variants** for user theme preference; they won’t respond to `data-theme="dark"` in this repo.
- Avoid hardcoded colors/opacity tricks that won’t be updated by theme CSS. If you need new styling tokens, add matching overrides in **both** `dark.css` and `colourful.css` (and ensure the default/standard theme still looks good).

## Quick example

- ✅ Prefer: `className="bg-white text-gray-900 border border-gray-300"`
- ❌ Avoid: `className="dark:bg-gray-800 dark:text-white"`
